Comment (internal/service/relational/workflows/seedimport.go:191):
**Symptom of the soft-delete upsert bug (see line 469): every re-import of a previously-deleted definition fails here.**

`SyncFilterForDefinition` → `WorkflowDefinitionService.GetByID` → `First(...)` applies GORM's default `deleted_at IS NULL` scope. When the upserted row is still soft-deleted (because the upsert didn't clear `deleted_at`), `GetByID` returns `record not found`, this returns an error, and the per-definition transaction at line ~125 rolls back — so the definition is counted as `failed` and nothing persists.

Reproduced on the running stack: import the seed, delete one definition, re-import the same file → `20 updated, 1 failed`, and the single failure is exactly the deleted definition, with:
```
sync workflow filter for seed definition "<key>": failed to load workflow definition: workflow definition with id <uuid> not found
```
A clean first-ever import works (fresh `deleted_at IS NULL` insert); the bug only bites re-import/reseed after any delete — which also breaks `make load-workflows` once a def has been removed.
